44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the meaning of the name of the constellation Cygnus?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cygnus is Latin for swan. Its bright stars also form the Northern Cross, a prominent asterism.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7bd5-a6da-463cfe2c381b","description":"Swan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-780d-94a1-eb0efbd7a3fb","description":"Ring","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-74da-bf04-64d5c323eb00","description":"River","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-76cd-97ab-42f2eb990cbb","description":"Mountain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-79d8-bb05-eae15e7cd1e9","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"Although the Poodle is widely associated with France, in which country is it believed to have originated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Poodle\u2019s name is linked to the word \u201cPudel,\u201d referring to splashing in water; the breed was developed as a water retriever.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-78a7-8209-0e93829cd16c","description":"Germany","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-74ff-a5e3-9dc5e1ea5a12","description":"Egypt","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-78ef-bac9-2aa42eff2493","description":"India","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7bc0-bbed-83b7db07401b","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7e0a-a733-d417f39c97b7","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was built by CERN near Geneva?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"CERN\u2019s Large Hadron Collider lies beneath the French-Swiss border and lets scientists study matter through high-energy collisions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7cd5-83c1-34805413cddb","description":"Particle accelerator","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7172-864c-e84794d0ba86","description":"Art museum","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-766d-9817-57894ccef62e","description":"Colossus computer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7fe8-b14f-107779801b9f","description":"Rocket launch pad","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7a03-81d5-de52c776c956","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was Rubik\'s Cube originally called when Ern\u0151 Rubik invented it in 1974?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Magic Cube was developed as a teaching tool for three-dimensional geometry before it was marketed internationally under Rubik\u2019s name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-75fa-adcf-3ec4d2f9a926","description":"Magic Cube","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-78e2-8e9c-951516b33e4c","description":"Wonder Cube","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7449-887e-032e9e7b8f91","description":"Hungarian Box","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7488-bbca-0d3ca6c1c7df","description":"Colour Block","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7e2b-9a1c-b24a0e15bc03","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"According to the biblical story of Cain and Abel, what type of animals did Abel offer as a sacrifice to God?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Genesis says Abel brought the firstborn of his flock as an offering, identifying the animals as sheep.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7376-b388-b239c7b6a2a3","description":"Sheep","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-731f-8983-0107e8f581e2","description":"Cows","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7141-bae0-3a85b993bf45","description":"Pigs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7586-b708-f46959ca0ff0","description":"Chickens","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-75a6-ae64-b4e28a70dc2d","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What metal corresponds to the Spanish term \"plata\"?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Spanish word plata means silver; the element\u2019s chemical symbol, Ag, comes from the Latin argentum.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-787c-abed-cab75bd04417","description":"Silver","correc