One Hundred and One Dalmatians gives 101; subtracting Snow White\'s seven dwarfs leaves 94.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-78f3-87aa-d0b77f224ac2","description":"94","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7dd9-a92f-c23bec9c890c","description":"97","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7d2a-bf35-791f820987ae","description":"89","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7fd3-8ebc-05b13a89d0b1","description":"91","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7174-b61e-8f0f8139e0e0","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What type of structures are used to conduct a water stream across a valley?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Aqueducts often relied on gravity to move water, and their elevated arches let channels cross valleys without following the terrain.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7a84-b318-7aa989625454","description":"Aqueducts","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7bff-9031-b5b93549ce1f","description":"Canals","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7ec7-99b3-21ec56193cdf","description":"Pipelines","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-72f9-b9c2-18fc2cdad12b","description":"Trenches","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-76ed-85c4-506d3612313f","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the Latin term for \"the arm\"?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bracchium is the source of the anatomical adjective brachial, as in the brachial artery.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7668-b21e-4d86eeffd9e5","description":"Bracchium","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-706c-b18e-c52362e18fac","description":"Caput","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7ac7-bdb2-4921a7634bc6","description":"Pedis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7bc6-bd83-2e9adf8c858a","description":"Oculus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-74e2-b98b-67124e57ca30","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the troy system of weights used to measure?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The troy system is used to measure precious metals. A troy ounce is about 31.1 grams, compared with about 28.35 grams for the everyday avoirdupois ounce.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7562-9c6b-47f981ac273b","description":"Precious metals","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7be1-b90f-15ccf8c9f154","description":"Radiation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-7179-855d-de928baf0c30","description":"Grain harvests","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3e-727a-9afc-cac0c22af75a","description":"Liquid fuels","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-7a68-92f7-21600e465892","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"In January 2018, which retail chain that kids love announced it would close about 180 stores?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Toys \"R\" Us announced the closures as part of a restructuring after filing for bankruptcy in 2017.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-7cb2-92da-304224a4f647","description":"Toys \"R\" Us","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-7e96-af83-10a96181ebc5","description":"Target","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-7a9e-b1eb-3a6b7c11577a","description":"Walmart","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-71ef-aa5f-d610981136e6","description":"Amazon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-77f0-a033-65820af6cc4b","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"On which date is the Feast of St. Nicholas celebrated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Feast of St. Nicholas is celebrated on December 6. St. Nicholas was a 4th-century bishop of Myra whose generosity helped inspire the gift-giving figure of Santa Claus.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-7240-8a03-bd54dbed9020","description":"December 6","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-7e89-99e1-72a104b1305e","description":"December 18","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae3f-7a22-ad5a-b46e57d163ec","description":"December 25","correct_answ